🌐 HTML (Hyper Text Markup Language) – Complete Note
🔹 What is HTML?

H → Hyper (Reference / Link)
T → Text (Data / Info)
M → Markup (Predefined / Marked Structure)
L → Language (Communication tool for browser)

👉 Definition:
HTML হলো একটি markup language যেটা ওয়েবপেজকে গঠন (structure) দেয়।

🔹 HTML Elements & Tags

✔️ All HTML Tags = Elements

<p> → Paragraph

<b> → Bold (Non-semantic)

<strong> → Bold + Important (Semantic ✅)

<i> → Italic (Non-semantic)

<em> → Emphasis, extra focus (Semantic ✅)

<span> → Specific inline styling/content

<small> → ছোট, হালকা টেক্সট

🔹 Headings

👉 <h1> to <h6> → বড় থেকে ছোট heading

<h1>Main Title</h1>
<h2>Sub Title</h2>
<h3>Section Title</h3>

🔹 Block vs Inline Elements

Block Tags → p, h1-h6, div

Inline Tags → strong, em, i, small, span

💡 Example:

<p>This is a paragraph (Block)</p>
<span>This is span (Inline)</span>

❓ Q1: Example of Block and Inline tag?

✅ Answer:

Block → <div>, <p>, <h1>

Inline → <span>, <strong>, <em>

❓ Q2: What is Semantic Tag? Why used?

✅ Answer:

Semantic tags are meaningful tags → যেমন <header>, <footer>, <article>, <section>, <strong>, <em>

These tell browser & search engines what content means (SEO + Accessibility)।

🔹 HTML Lists
1️⃣ Unordered List (ul)
<ul type="disc">
  <li>Biryani</li>
  <li>Borhani</li>
  <li>Kala Bhuna</li>
  <li>Salt-Lemon</li>
</ul>


Types → disc, circle, square, none

2️⃣ Ordered List (ol)
<ol>
  <li>Liton</li>
  <li>Taskin</li>
  <li>Shanto</li>
  <li>Tamim</li>
</ol>

3️⃣ Description List (dl)
<dl>
  <dt>HTML</dt>
  <dd>HyperText Markup Language, the structure of the web.</dd>
</dl>

🔹 Important HTML Tags

<div> → Division/Container

<br> → Line Break

<button> → Clickable Button

🔹 Anchor Tag <a>
<a href="https://www.google.com" target="_blank">Google</a>


👉 Parts:

<a> → Start Tag

href → Attribute Name

"https://..." → Attribute Value

Google → Affected Content

</a> → End Tag

Extra → target, download attribute

🔹 Image Tag <img>
<img src="img.jpg" alt="Description of image">


Self-closing / void tag

alt → accessibility (if image not load)

Internal vs External images

🔹 Input Tag
<input type="text">
<input type="email">
<input type="password">
<input type="date">
<input type="file">
<input type="submit">

❓ Q3: What are different types of input in HTML?

✅ Answer:

text, email, password, number, date, file, checkbox, radio, submit, button, color, range, url, tel ইত্যাদি।

🔹 HTML Structure
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>My Website</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="favicon.ico">
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>Hello HTML</h1>
    <p>This is my first website</p>
  </body>
</html>

🔹 Common Sections in HTML5

<header> → Top section

<nav> → Navigation

<main> → Main content

<article> → Article content

<section> → Grouped content

<footer> → Copyright / Contact

🔹 Extra Notes

! + Shift → Auto HTML boilerplate (Emmet shortcut)

Favicon → website icon (in browser tab)

Comments in HTML:

<!-- This is a comment, not visible in UI -->

🟢 Summary

✅ HTML → Structure of webpage
✅ Tags = Elements
✅ Inline vs Block → Layout difference
✅ Semantic tags → Meaningful, SEO friendly
✅ Lists → ul, ol, dl
✅ Form Inputs → বিভিন্ন ধরণের data collect করার জন্য
✅ Boilerplate → doctype + html + head + body